// The chess Knight can move two squares horizontally, then one square vertically, or 
// two squares vertically then one square horizontally in the chessboard as long as the 
// final square it reaches is empty (as shown in the example figure). Design a greedy 
// algorithm in the form of pseudo-code to find the minimum length path by which a 
// Knight can move from one corner of an 8 × 8 chessboard to the diagonally opposite 
// corner (the length of a path is measured by the number of squares it passes through 
// including the first and the last squares). Then, find its order of growth. 


chessboard(start, target)
    current = start;
    mark current as visited
    bestMove=NULL
    bestDistance=INFINITY
    while (current != target)
        for each possible move m from current  
            if m is inside board and not visited
                d = EuclideanDistance(m, target)
                if d<bestDistance
                    bestDistance=d
                    bestMove = m
        current = bestMove;
        mark current as visited
        length++


    return length